{#- Follows infloww.com/complaints-policy. -#}
<h2>How to complain</h2>
<ol>
  <li><a href="{{ site.repo }}/issues/new">Open an issue</a> on the repository.</li>
  <li>Say what is wrong and where: a page on this site, a file in the repository, or the app's behaviour.</li>
  <li>The maintainers answer in the issue, where you can follow it.</li>
</ol>
<p>
  Infloww's policy promises an investigation "within seven (7) business days"
  (infloww.com/complaints-policy, page stamped Oct 10, 2026). Ours promises a thread, and a reply to legal notices within 7 days (see below). Everything else gets an answer when a maintainer gets to it.
</p>

<h2>Content on this site</h2>
<p>
  If something here is wrong about Infloww or anyone else, or uses material it shouldn't, open an issue with the page
  and the line. We fix or remove it.
</p>
<p>
  Legal and trademark notices: open an issue on the repository; we reply within 7 days. There is no private notice channel yet; issues are public and need a free GitHub account, and they open when the repository does. A legal-notice address will be added before the repository goes public.
</p>

<h2>Content in someone's install</h2>
<p>
  The project hosts no app and no content. Each install runs on its operator's own server, so a complaint about what
  an install does goes to whoever runs it.
</p>

<h2>Keep secrets out</h2>
<p>
  Anyone who can see the repository can read its issues. Don't post tokens, <code>.env</code> files, session files or personal data. Describe the
  problem without them; there is no private channel yet.
</p>
